This file (README) describes the content of the folder in which it resides.
This folder is the top of the OpenJDK release, with additions for OpenJML.

OpenJDK material: (mostly consistent with 21-ga branch of OpenJDK)
src - source code for OpenJDK + OpenJML
doc - documentation files for OpenJDK
make - the makefiles for OpenJDK (only change for OpenJML is to add -g into build flags)
test - the test material for OpenJDK
ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO
ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION
configure
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
Makefile -- builds OpenJDK, with additional targets to build OpenJML
README.md -- brief OpenJDK documentation

OpenJML public executables (fixed scripts that reference build products)
openjml
openjml-java
openjml-compiler
openjml-run

OpenJML material
release-files - this folder holds files that are copied verbatim into an OpenJML release
setup-exports - an OpenJML script
version.sh - an OpenJML script
README - this file
README-OpenJML.txt -- brief OpenJLM documentation

Build results:
build - output build files for OpenJDK + OpenJML
jmlruntime.jar -- the OpenJML runtime libaray (used for RAC)

Folders that hold temporary output material:
release-temp -- folder used to stage material in creating a local release .zip file
tempDocs -- folder used to clone and build pdf files from LaTeX sources in OverLeaf
temp-release -- folder used to expand a release for testing
tempUserGuide -- folder used to stage user guide examples
templib -- folder used to stage the materials for jmlruntime.jar
